  "decisions": [
    "Small D64 output splitting and QK k_pack=1 do not provide stable gains over v4.",
    "IEEE reciprocal had hot-cache gains on seed 0 but regressions on seed 61 and cold-cache D64 tests. Not adopted.",
    "Wide-load vector128 is roughly half as fast as v4 on the four tested shapes.",
    "Wide-load vector64 and explicit vector loads are mostly neutral or mixed; no new candidate was assembled.",
    "Initial explicit-vector probes failed in Z3 Shuffle binding and nonconstant Shuffle codegen. Both failures were retained; no analyzer or race/bounds pass was disabled.",
    "The immutable release_v4 is byte-identical to candidate_v4 and contains none of these follow-up experiments."
  ]
}
